adjudication.rationale:
In `GitHubInstallation.dispatch`, the new authenticity check directly indexes `integration.metadata["sender"]["login"]` without any guards:
```py
if pipeline.fetch_state("github_authenticated_user") != integration.metadata["sender"]["login"]:
    return error(...)
```
If an existing `Integration` row has `metadata` missing `sender` (or `sender` missing `login`), this will raise `KeyError` and produce a 500 instead of the intended `error(...)` response. The diff adds this unhandled access and does not show any migration/backfill ensuring those keys always exist.
